Evaluating $\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ at $\blueD{\theta = \dfrac{\pi}{3}}$ gives us the slope of our tangent line.

$\begin{align}
\greenD{\left. \dfrac{dy}{dx}\right| _{\theta=\tfrac{\pi}{3}}}
&=\dfrac{2\sin\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{3}}\right)\cos^2\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{3}}\right)-\sin^3\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{3}}\right)}{\cos^3\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{3}}\right)-2\sin^2\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{3}}\right)\cos\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{3}}\right)} 
\\\\
&=\dfrac{2\left(\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)\left(\dfrac{1}{2}\right)^2-\left(\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)^3}{\left(\dfrac{1}{2}\right)^3-2\left(\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)^2\left(\dfrac{1}{2}\right)} 
\\\\
&=\dfrac{2\sqrt{3}-3\sqrt{3}}{1-6}
\\\\
&=\greenD{\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{5}}
\end{align}$
